<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 95,890 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 95,890 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 95,890 tonnes of export and import cargo in 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Monday, compared to 84,437 tonnes on in the previous 24 hours.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>					    Monday	   Previous</p>
<p>    Export cargo			11,115	   15,438</p>
<p>    Import cargo			84,775	   68,999</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, six ship sailed and five berthed. In the next 24 hours, four ships were expected to sail and nine were expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at the Karachi Port:</p>
<p>Commodity		Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		  Berthing</p>
<p>Soyabean oil	    7,850	 Petr Shmidt	15/11</p>
<p>High speed deisel    56,000	 Keefan		 due</p>
<p>Palm oil		  6,100	 Jianshe-33	 13/11</p>
<p>Tallow		   36,000	 Vanino	     25/11</p>
<p>High speed deisel    34,500	 Al-Deerah	    due</p>
<p>Crude oil		65,000	 Capitan Mirinda  16/11</p>
<p>Motor gasoline	 25,000	 Stavanger Pride    due</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
